+# Four-Node Master-Owned Recording Transfer
+
+## Scope
+
+This implementation supports the Master plus Nodes 1–4 in one recording
+session. Every source records locally. The Master writes its own binary directly
+to SD; each Node writes to external flash and uploads after recording.
+
+## Transfer ownership
+
+The Master owns Node upload control. The desktop HTML client observes and plots
+Node frames but does not issue ManifestAck, AckWindow, NackRange, Pause, or
+VerifyOk for Node sources. The existing browser-controlled transfer remains
+available for the Master's own source.
+
+## Sequence
+
+1. All selected Nodes must be transport-ready and recorder-ready.
+2. The Master sends PrepareRecord and waits for every selected Node.
+3. The Master sends CommitPreparedRecord and starts its local recorder.
+4. Each Node records to external flash.
+5. RecordDone messages are queued by the Master.
+6. Nodes upload sequentially in queue order, with one credit at a time.
+7. Every chunk is checked for source, session, offset, chunk index, bounds, and
+   CRC16 before being written.
+8. Exact duplicates are accepted only if they match the bytes already staged.
+9. Gaps and corrupt chunks generate NackRange without destroying the staged
+   file.
+10. The completed staged binary is checked using header CRC and payload CRC32.
+11. The Master sends VerifyOk only after the SD copy passes validation.
+12. The Node may erase flash only after VerifyOk.
+13. The Master converts the retained raw source file into the combined training
+    CSV, marks the source complete, and advances to the next Node.
+
+## Resume behavior
+
+A Node retains its session after disconnect. It periodically resends RecordDone.
+When the Master receives RecordDone for the active source and session, it
+resends ManifestAck. The Node keeps its existing upload cursor for the same
+session; the next AckWindow or NackRange re-establishes the exact contiguous
+position.
+
+## Durability rules
+
+- Raw Master and Node binaries remain on SD.
+- A Node is never erased on browser verification.
+- A forward gap is recoverable and does not immediately fail the session.
+- A mismatched duplicate, SD write failure, invalid header, or final CRC
+  mismatch remains a hard staging failure.
+- The combined CSV is complete only when the expected source mask is complete.
+
+## Validation
+
+The host test `Firmware/HostTests/test_master_node_transfer_window.cpp` covers
+sequential chunks, exact duplicates, forward gaps, corrupt payloads, wrong
+sources, final completion, and reset behavior.
+
+On-device acceptance still requires four programmed Nodes and the Master:
+
+- repeated short sessions;
+- five-minute sessions;
+- browser disconnect during Node ingestion;
+- Node disconnect/reconnect during upload;
+- deliberate RF interference;
+- long-duration soak testing;
+- SD-full and SD-write failure tests.
